London, 17 May 1995 CPMP/147/95
Opinion of the committee for proprietary medicinal products on the granting of a marketing authorization for
GONAL- F® proposed INN: Follitropin alpha 75 IU lyophilisate for injection 3 ml, 1 or 3 or 5 or 10 vials subcutaneous
BASIS FOR OPINION
In application of Article 2 of Directive 93/41/EEC the company Serono Laboratories (UK) Limited submitted to the EMEA on 13 January 1995 an application concerning the abovementioned prod­uct which falls within the scope of Part A of the Annex to Council Regulation (EC) 2309/93 of 22 July 1993.
Written explanations have been provided on 12 April 1995.
The Committee, having considered the application as stated in the appended evaluation report, is in favour of granting a marketing authorization for the abovementioned medicinal product in accord­ance with the proposed summary of product characteristics in Annex I.
Proposed manufacturing or importing conditions and conditions or restrictions of supply and use, are stated in Annex 2.
Proposed labelling and user package leaflet are given in Annex 3.
The present opinion, together with its annexes and appendices, is forwarded to the Commission, to Member States' competent authorities and to the applicant.
London, 17 May 1995.
Prof. J. M. Alexandre, Chairman, on behalf of the CPMP
