If you administer GONAL- F' yourself, please carefully read the following instructions:
It is important that your hands and the items you use be as clean as possible.
Push the plunger until the air bubbles are gone.
Assemble everything you need: find a clean area and lay out everything (two alcohol swabs, one diluent ampoule, the vial containing the medication, one syringe, one needle for reconstitution and a fine bore needle for subcutaneous injection).
Your doctor or nurse will have already advised you where to inject (e.g. tummy, front of thigh).
Wipe the chosen area with an alcohol swab.
Firmly pinch the skin together and insert the needle at a 45" to 90° angle using a dart-like motion.
Inject under the skin, as you were taught.
Do not inject directly into a vein.
Inject the solution by pushing gently on the plunger.
Take as much time as you need to inject all the solution.
Immediately withdraw the needle and clean the skin with an alcohol swab using a circular motion.
• Open the ampoule of diluent: On the head of the diluent ampoule, you will see a small coloured dot.
Directly below it is where the neck of the ampoule has been treated to make it easier to break.
Gently flick the top sec tion of the ampoule so that any fluid in the neck of the ampoule drops into the bottom chamber.
Now press the ampoule firmly over the neck, and break the ampoule away from the coloured dot.
Carefully place the open ampoule upright on the work surface.
The effects of an overdose of GONAL- F" are unknown, nevertheless one could expect ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome to occur, which is further described in 'Undesirable Effects'.
UNDESIRABLE EFFECTS
