Carefully set the syringe down on the work surface, taking care not to touch the needle.
Local reactions at the injection site (pain, redness and bruising), have been observed in some cases.
Open and prepare the injection solution: Remove the protective cap from the GONAL- F® powder vial, pick up your syringe and slowly inject the diluent into the vial of GONAL- F" powder.
Following treatment with GONAL- F® when human chorionic gonadotrophin is administered, a condition called ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome (see also 'Special warnings') can occur.
