The Centre's Annual Report on the State of the Drugs Problem in the European Union (this publication is a summary of the 1997 report) is its main informa­tion dissemination vehicle.
Much of the data for the report derives directly or indirectly from the EMCDDA's partners in the national focal points of the 15 Member States and in the European Commis­sion, or from the EMCDDA's six priority international partners.
The core problem with which the EMCDDA and its partners grapple is ensuring the availability and comparability of information from varied na­tional data collection systems embedded in diver­gent cultures and administrative structures.
