Work Programmes
Every three years, the EMCDDA Management Board adopts a Three­year Work Programme for the Centre.
Each year, it also adopts an annual Work Programme and budget.
The first three years (1995­97)
It contains comprehensive information on all aspects of the Centre and its products, from an overview of its origins and administrative structure to details of its epide­miological, demand­reduction and REITOX Work Programmes.
In addition, the site includes: EMCDDA publications in full text or with des­criptions and ordering information; a full list of staff contacts; and links to the REITOX Focal Points and other related web sites.
The Centre is developing a set of epidemiological indicators to provide standardised and comparable information on drug use in the European Union.
The five key indicators cover: demand for treat­ment by drug users; drug­related deaths and mortality among drug users; infectious diseases among drug injectors; drug use in the general population; and prevalence estimates of problem drug use.
In addition, these data are being used for more in­depth analyses and interpretation using qualitative and quantitative methods.
