The EMCDDA's Documentation and Information Centre (DIC) consists of a specialised library and an electronic information service linked to the REITOX network.
Its bibliographical database contains references to over 2,700 documents, including those of the EMCDDA's technical and scientific reports, the National Reports compiled by the REITOX Focal Points, and documents published by the European Union institutions.
As a step towards creating a pan­European Information Network on Drugs and Drug Addiction, the DIC, in co­operation with the Focal Points, has developed a 'virtual library'accessible through the Internet.
The DIC caters to the information needs of the EMCDDA, its partners and other users.
On 16 June 1997, the EMCDDA was assigned a key role in the detection and assessment of new synthetic drugs in the European Union under the terms of a Joint Action formally adopted in Brussels by the Council of the European Union.
