There is widespread recognition of the need for alternatives to custody for drug users especially forfirst or minor offences,with treatment options inprison complementing alternatives to custody.These schemes have been cost-effective and aresensitive mechanisms for providing alternatives tothe drug escalations(and consequent public healthconcerns) that have occurred when addicts are simply incarcerated.
