1 GENERAL INTRODUCTION
In accordance with Article 10 (3) of the Financial Regulation of the Translation Centre, this supplementary and amending budget for 1998 reflects changes in both revenue and expenditure which have occurred in the course of the year.
For work other than translation work, the price is set at ECU 780 per man-day.
The changes in revenue are as follows:
Article 1000:
I) Reduction of ECU 60,000 in the payment from the European Environment Agency.
4) Reduction of ECU 450,000 in the payment from the European Agency for the Evaluation of Medicinal Products. II) Increase of ECU 57,000 in the payment from CEDEFOP.
12) Increase of ECU 72,000 in the payment from the European Monetary Institute/European Central Bank.
13) Payment of ECU 30,000 from the European Monitoring Centre on Racism and Xenophobia.
Article 1002:
1) Release by the European Parliament of appropriations amounting to ECU 450,000 from the reserve under heading A 4015 of the General Budget, intended for institutional cooperation in the translation field, and payment of ECU 300,000 from heading B2-702 (Commission), intended to finance the translation of the JARs for DG VII.
2) Increase of ECU 67,000 in the payment from the European Court of Auditors.
3) Creation of a token entry item for the Council of the European Union.
The balance resulting from these changes is ECU 466,000; this is intended to cover the following expenditure:
"Freelance services", a sum of ECU 216,000 to finance the increase in the number of pages to be translated arising from the changes listed above.
"Services provided by data-processing staff", a sum of ECU 250,000 to Finance feasibility studies on an interinstitutional terminological database.
