Although your Commission already started the investigations we herewith comply as yet with your request to interested parties (96/c 6O/01 - 29 February 1996) to make a contribution to support your activities.
ECASBA, the European arm of The Federation of National Associations of Ship Brokers and Agents (FONASBA), exists specifically to provide a contact point with the European Commission and those of its directorates that have a shipping involvement.
The ship agent is the representative of the ship owner or charterer and acts as middleman between the shipping line and the cargo interests.
Since the development worldwide of container transports, the ship owner and his agent or agency department got involved more and more in landtransport.
Moreover the container has facilitated the hub principle with the result that transhipment of containers to other nearby ports is put into practice on a large scale.
On top of that the internal market was introduced (1993) with the result that internal borders were abolished.
In that respect sea ports, being the points of entry of the Community, have become a main target for customs control.
Altogether it means that the ship agent has more to do with customs transit procedures than in the past.
But also for the on-carriage by sea the community transit system is applicable.
Whereas existing legislation contains many gaps and is unable to effectively guarantee the Community's own resources and national taxes".
