* Club members must ato use "approved hauliers" who must fulfil the contract requirements of the "Club" to qualify for "approval"
* "Approved agents" are allocated a temporary unique PIN Reference as per "Approved" Club Members and details of their own specified security identifiers are ato held.
Temporary status L· held for a period of 6 months, during which time a physical audit of the dhcharge documentation L· made together with a reliability assessment of the agent If after the trial approval period the agent L· found to be performing to the standards required, the temporary status of the PIN Reference will be made permanent and the agents detaUs added to the file of "approved" agents.
Outline Procedure.
* Validity period for UCR to be used with a Departure A dvice of Transit message (DA T)
* UCR automatically cancelled and "Club" member advised if DA Τ message not received within validity period of UCR
* DA Τ detaiL· and Estimated Time of Arrival (ETA) advised to "approved agent" in country of destination (can aho be advised to Customs -for further detaiL·, see section 6, Interfacing with Customs)
* Immediately on arrival of the transit consignment at the office of destination, the "approved agent" sends an "Arrival Advice of Transit" (AA T) message to the system
* If the system does not receive an AA Τ message within the ETA, the system will automatically advise the originator of the DA Τ and appropriate "approved agent" of the fact and will continue to automatically send the message every 2 hours until either the ETA L· amended or the AA Τ message L· received (this message can ato be sent to Customs - see section 6)
The system will record all instances of failure to receive AA Τ messages niihin the ETA and will call for explanations from the "approved agent".
Consistent failure to. input AA Τ messages within the ETA period will be reported to the "Club" for their decision on whether the "approved agent" should retain access to the system or not
These control and reporting procedures ato apply to the update status of the AA Τ message.
* Following receipt of the AAT message, the system applies a "time out" period which L· specified by the originator of the DA Τ message, in which the "approved agent" must update the status of the AAT message with the details of the Custom's reference which signify that the transit has been taken under their control (the update status message can ato be sent to Customs - see section 6)
* During the probationary period, "approved agents" must submit copies of the documentation used to update the AA Τ message, to the specified central independent control office in the country of destination. Checks will be in order to ratify the veracity of the update status of the AA Τ message
* Where thL· check L· satisfactory, the system will generate a Transaction Message (TCM) which will update the transaction file
