A motion of censure on the Commission may be submitted to the President byone tenth of the component Members of Parliament.
The motion shall be called 'motionof censure'and supportedby reasons. ltshall be forwarded to the Commission.
The President shall announce to Members that a motion of censure has beentabled immediately he receivesit. it.
The debate on the motion shall not take place until at least 24 hours after itsreceipt is announced to Members.
The vote on the motion shall be by roll call and shall not be taken until at least48 hours after the beginning of the debate.
The debate and the vote shall take place, at the latest, during the part-sessionfollowingthe submission of the motion.
The motion of censure shall be adopted if it securesa two-thirds majority of thevotes cast, representing a majority of the component Members of Parliament.
Theresult of the vote shall be notified to the President of the Council and the Presidentof the Commission.
