Rule 76Time limits
The President shall, at the request of the delegation, ask the Council to agree toan extension,by a maximum of two weeks,of the six-week periods allowed for thework of the Conciliation Committee and for the approval of a joint text or the rejection of a Council text.
The President may, after consultation with the delegation,agree on behalf of Parliament to a request from the Council for an extension,by a maximum of twoweeks, of the six-week periods mentioned in paragraph 1.
