Rule 82Official codification of Community legislation
When a Commission proposal for official codification of Community legislation issubmitted to Parliament, it shall be referred to the committee responsible for legalmatters. Provided that it is ascertained that the proposal does not entail any changeof substanceto existing Community legislation, the procedure laid down in Rule143(1)shall be followed.
The chairman of the committee responsible or the rapporteur appointed by thatcommittee may participatein the examination and revisionof the proposal forcodification. lf necessary, the committee responsible may give its opinionbeforehand.
Notwithstanding the provisions of Rule 143(3), the procedure without report maynot be applied to a proposal for official codification where this procedure is opposedby a majority of the members of the committee responsible for legal matters or ofthe committee responsible.
Consequences of the Council failing to act following approval of its commonposition lf, within three or, with the agreement of the Council, four months of thecommunication of the common position, Parliament has neither rejected noramended the position, and the Council fails to adopt the proposed legislation inaccordance with the common position, the President may, on behalf of Parliamentand after consulting the committee responsible for legal affairs,bring an actionagainst the Council in the Court of Justice under Article175 of the EC Treaty.
Rule 84Proceedings before the Court of Justice
Parliament shall, within the time limits specified by the Treaties and the Statuteof the Court of Justice for action by the institutions of the Union and by any naturalor legal persons, examine Community legislation to ensure that its rights have beenfully respected.
The committee responsible shall report to Parliament, orally if necessary, whereit suspects a breach of Parliament's rights.
