Rule 87Parliamentary control over implementation of the budget
Parliament shall monitorthe implementation of the current year's budget. lt shallentrust this task to the committee responsible for budgetary control and the other committees concerned.
Each year it shall, however, consider, before the first reading of the draft budgetfor the following financial year, the problems involved in the implementation of thecurrent budget, where appropriate on the basis of a motion for a resolution tabled by its committee responsible.
