Rule 143Procedure without report - simplified procedure
At each committee meeting the chairman shall submit to the committee a list ofthe proposals which in his opinionancl/or at the President's recommendation should be approved without report.
The chairman shall put each proposal on the list to the committee for decision.Unless at least four members object, the chairman of the committee shall inform the
At the recommendation of the President or following a proposal from itschairman, the committee may deliver its views on a proposal in accordance with the simplified procedure.
Unless at least four members object to this procedure, the committee chairman shallbe deemed to have been appointed rapporteur.
The draft report, consistingof aprocedural section, a draft legislative resolution and a brief explanatory statement, shall be sentto the members of the committee. Unless at least four members of thecommittee object within a set time limit,which may not be less than fourteen daysfrom the date of dispatch,the report shall be considered as having been adopted by the committee.
3. lf at least four members object to the procedure referred to in paragraphs 1 or 2,the procedure provided for in Rule 144 (procedure with report)shall be followed.
Rule 144Gommittee reports on consultations
The chairman of the committee to which a Commission proposal has beenreferred shall propose to the committee the procedure to be followed.
Following a decision on the procedure to be followed,and if Rule 143 does notapply, the committee shall appoint a rapporteur on the Commission proposal fromamong its members or permanent substitutes if it has not yet done so on the basisof the annual legislative programme agreed under Rule49. 49.
The committee's report shall comprise:a) draft amendments, if any, to the proposal;b) a draft legislative resolution, in accordance with Rule58(2); 58(2); c) an explanatory statement
Rule 145Non-le$slative reports
Where a committeedraws up a non-legislative report, it shall appoint arapporteur from among its members or permanent substitutes.
The rapporteur shall be responsible for preparing the committee's report and forpresenting it to Parliament on behalf of the committee.
The committee's report shall comprise:a) a motion for a resolution;b) an explanatorystatement; statement; c) the tefis of any motions for resolutions to be included under Rule 45(4).
Rule 146Explanatory statements and deadlines ines
The explanatory statement shall be the responsibility of the rapporteur and shallnot be put to the vote. lt must, however,accord with the text of the motion for aresolution as adopted and any amendments proposed by the committee and shall,where necessary, give a clear indication of the minorityopinion. opinion.
The report shall state the result of the vote taken on the report as a whole.
Inaddition, if, when the vote is taken, at least one third of the members present so request, the report shall indicate how each member voted.
Where the committee's opinion is not unanimous the report shall also give asummary of the minorityopinion. opinion.
On a proposalfrom its bureau, a committee may set a deadline within which therapporteur shall submit his draft report.
This deadline may be extended.
The debates may then be conductedon the basis of an oral report by the committee concerned.
Rule 147Opinions of committees
The committee asked for an opinion shall communicatethe opinion to thecommittee responsible either orally, through its chairman or draftsman, or in writing.
Its opinion shall relateto the text referred to it.
In its report the committee responsible shall set out the views of the committeeasked for an opinion, insofaras these differ from itsown. own.
The committee asked for an opinion must deliver it within the time limit set bythe committee responsible so that it may be taken into account when voting therepod in committee.
The committee responsible shall not reach its final conclusionsbefore that time limit has expired.
The opinion may include amendments to the text referred to the committee andsuggestions for parts of the motion for a resolution submitted by the committeeresponsiblebu,t shall notincludeany motionfor a resolutionas such.
