Rule 150Procedure in committee
A committee may validlyvote when one quarter of its members are actuallypresent.
However, if so requested by one sixth of its members before voting begins,the vote shall be valid only if the majority of the component members of thecommittee have taken part in it.
Voting in committee shall be by show of hands, unless a quarter of thecommittee's members request a vote by roll call.
The chairman may take part in discussions and may vote, but without having acasting vote.
