In the sphete of foreign relations, Parliament exercises a genuine power of ratification, giving its assent to accession and association agreements.
The Treaty on European Union has also extended this procedure to cover the uniform electoral law, the Structural Funds and European citizenship.
This undoubtedly strengthens Parliament's powers.
Parliament will, for example, appint a European Ombudsman towhom the citizens of the Union will have the right to appeal.
Moreover, citizens will continue to enjoy the right to appeal to Parliament through its Committee on Petitions.
THE EUROPEAN INSTITUTIONS
The European Union is made up of democratic States.
A democracy without a parliament is inconceivable; this is why the European Parliament was created.
Country by country, Parliament's make­up today is as follows:
The European Parliament has three places of work Luxembourg, Brussels and Strasbourg.
Parliament's petmanent seat has been freed in Sttasbourg, where it meets each month in oidinary plenary sessions for one week.
