To this end, we must all unite in a Union that sets an example in terms of political, social and geographical cohesion.
It will not suffice to set up a bazaar, a market where people go only to gain economic advantages at others' expense; what is needed is a community, based on the pursuit of the common interest, guided by democratic institutions and inspired by a firm commitment to integration.
This is, beyond doubt, another of the key challenges facing the Intergovernmental Conference, which will have to pay very careful attention to such matters of major public concern as unemployment - I repeat - and social exclusion, the environment and the health of EU citizens.
Secondly, the Minutes do not record that I objected to the procedure, as you requested, and you then ignored that objection.
