My intention is to restore the dynamism of the single market with specific, priority proposals de signed to make good all the existing shortcomings.
I must not pass over the passage in the ministerial declaration which refers to the initiative on behalf of the less developed countries, because it was the Commission's efforts in Singapore that ensured that the initiative was not simply buried.
It is true that neither the question of relations between trade and environment nor that of basic social standards saw the breakthrough for which the Commission was hoping.
I remain convinced that the future will enable us to press forward with our ideas, as indeed we can do here and now in the other two areas in which the Union is keenly interested: relations between trade and investment, and relations between trade and national competition rules.
