Lindqvist (ELDR), in writing. - (SV) Common view points arrived at through interstate agreement are a better way of resolving the issues taken up in Article Kl in the long term, than decisions adopted by a qualified majority.
Immigration, asylum and visa policies must be better coordinated.
This ought to happen through unanimous decisions and not by majority decision.
