ance from the Commission and enshrinement of the principle for selecting the most beneficial or least prejudicial measures for the environment are - as Mr Hatzidakis says - fundamental factors for making progress on the road to a Community regional policy increasingly com mitted to our environment and with the already established principle of sustainable development.
Fernández Martín (PPE). - (ES) Madam President, Madam Commissioner, to avoid repetition, I will just emphasize a few points:
