President. Question No 66 by Caroline Jackson (H­1039/96)
Subject: Food additives and public information
Article 8 of Directive 94/36/EC (') states that the Commission will undertake a programme of public information so that toe significance of toe most fre­quently used Ε­numbers, indicating the presence of particular additives, will be better known.
Mr Bange­mann stated in July 1996 that a study on this subject had bçen completed. What has happened to it, and what does the Commission plan to do next on this subject?
Technically speaking, would the Commissioner not agree that the Commission is in breach of the law.
