governed by the aims of completing the internal market and harmonizing health protection.
As far as Parliament is concerned, the knowledge and experience we have amassed in the last few weeks and months show that the only appropriate legal basis is Article 100a in conjunction with Article 129a.
I am also thinking particularly of Mr Mayer's comments here, which I fully endorse, when he said that we should extend toe scope of this legal basis to take in the other two reports being presented to us today.
