McCartin (PPE), draftsman of the opinion of the Com mittee on Budgetary Control. - Madam President, yesterday we were expressing the concerns of European con sumers and consumers outside toe Union on the whole question of beef.
Today we are taking appropriate measures to meet some of those concerns.
I welcome the new urgency and activity of toe European Commission in this area.
I reject the criticism that this proposal imposes unnecessary administrative costs on farmers.
It is absolutely necessary to do this to consoUdate the markets which European farmers have for their meat products.
It is necessary also to reassure people in third countries who buy our products.
