Amadeo (NT). - (IT) Madam President, the globalization of trade which raises the level of knowledge, the arrival·of the information society which will radically transform the nature of work and the organization of production, to gether with the acceleration of technical and scientific progress are the scenarios of the future, obliging the Union to reflect now on how it can respond adequately to the new demands of the world of work and education.
The Member States must make an effort providing schools with the required computer equipment so that multimedia education is available to all, since many families, for obvious economic reasons, are not able to buy multimedia equipment.
