(2) The problem of subsidy shopping in the EC has still to be resolved. As we in this Parliament, particularly on the basis of Green initiatives, have repeatedly stated, it is high time we ensured that all European and national location grants are linked to longterm sectoral and regional development plans and that they are made repayable in the event of a company reneging on its commitment.
Last week's Europe-wide strike is a real gesture of awareness by the workforce in favour of social Europe.
The soüdarity of the French and Spanish workers with their Belgian coUeagues is something new!
It is time we shifted the focus of this debate on European industry policies to consider how we can restructure car manufacturing into a mobility industry - and there have been moves in this direction, but where these occur they are pushed back down the agenda.
