The Fisheries Council was only held five days ago and the Commission undertook to evaluate the political feasibility of a new proposal.
The Commission does not intend to give anyone an alibi by presenting another proposal if the same conditions of political deadlock exist.
That would simply be another two years of research, study and analysis, which would not lead anywhere.
The Com mission will only do it if it is sure the conditions for another, equivalent political deadlock are no longer there.
President. - Thank you very much, Mrs Bonino.
