Brittan, Sir Leon, Vice-President of the Commission. -Given the understanding reached between the Commission and the United States and the commitments undertaken in it by the United States, the Council agreed that the cunent WTO panel proceedings in'respect of the Helms-Burton Libertad legislation will now be suspended but, if action is taken against EU companies or individuals under the Libertad Act or under the Iran and Libya Sanctions Act or waivers as described in the understanding are not granted or withdrawn, the Commission will request the WTO to restart or re-establish the panel which will then follow its 'natural course.
