Etti arrangements - possibly in the future Economic and Financial Committee or in some other way - with the European Central Bank.
I do not consider it appropriate in that context always to be talking in terms of black and white, of hard and soft currencies, particularly when, in the background, we are considering and fixing exchange rate mechanisms.
What is actually needed is to create a stable currency that meets our needs in the global currency context.
That is what we are aiming for.
for the preparatory work that was done by the European Monetary Institute and its president, Mr Lamfalussy, as this will provide a sound basis on which to build further, However, recent developments illustrate just how critical the situation is.
