These reports fully follow the general direction taken, which we opposed, but which we think does contain some positive points, which might help in this new situation as regards the reflection which is so urgently needed.
We must and can now open the way to a Monetary Union within the framework of which it will at least be possible to resolve the major structural problems that were simply concealed by the previous policy of casino­style capital­ism that was all show and no substance: the unemploy­ment problem, the environmental crisis ­ when do we now hear anyone talk about the Rio principles and commitments and the Delors promises? ­ but also the problem of real and not just monetary convergence be­tween our Member States.
