Ewing (ARE). - Mr President, I would thank Mrs Randzio-Plath foT her radical rethink on the VAT system which is a very cumbersome arrangement and does not seem to have been designed for the Single Market.
In truth, the single currencies creates more problems than it solves and everyone knows that full well. It calls for a considerable increase in the European budget in order to deal with asymmetrical economic shocks; Mr Fourçans recalled that earlier.
