Those programmes are in tended to be only 50% EU-funded; ECU 15 m is earmarked for this in the EU budget, with the bulk of that - ECU 11.6 m - being destined for measures to combat bee diseases.
In conclusion, the Commission welcomes the achievement of the Conciliation Committee which has enhanced the common position and takes into account the important amendments by the European Parliament at second read ing.
The final text boosts the Community aspect of the directive and improves consumer protection.
Read (PSE), rapporteur. - Madam President, can I thank the Commissioner but just query one small point in his presentation?
Commissioner Fischler, our feelings range from disap pointment to anger at the lack of understanding shown for the difficult position of commercial or part-time beekeepers, and the serious consequences for agriculture and the environment if not enough bees are raised to ensure that the pollination that is so important from both an ecological and an economic point of view takes place.
