Väyrynen (ELDR). - (FI) Mr President, Mr Burenstam Linder has tabled a very good report on Baltic cooperation.
I congratulate him on it. On behalf of the Liberal Group I have tabled two additional amendments referring to cooperation in the Barents Sea area.
They are based on the report by Mr Tindemans adopted in May.
But, of course, the bulk of the report and the debate ought to be about Baltic Sea regional cooperation.
There I beg to differ from Mrs Ojala, who has somewhat understated the extent of the involvement of the European Union in general and the Commission in particular in that process.
