Telkämper (V). - (DE) Mr President, once again we have tens of thousands of deaths to lament in Congo/BrazzaviUe, and here we are discussing the conflict.
What I wonder is whether we could not conduct the sort of active policy that would prevent these hostilities and these deaths.
During the past six days all heU has been let loose in a country we once regarded as exemplary because its President, who himself initiated the democratization process in 1989, was peacefully voted out of office in 1992.
