IN THE CHAIR: MRS FONTAINE Vice-President
(The sitting was opened at 9.00 a.m.) (') ments, changed their flights and so on. It seems to me -and this is my personal opinion, the Conference of Presidents may, of course, look at the question again - but I think it would be extremely strange to alter our agenda so abrupdy by missing a morning's plenary session.
I do not doubt for an instant that after the powerful plea you have just made, Mr Hallam, all our colleagues here will be intent on attending the presentation of your report, to which I strongly invite them.
Are there any comments?
(The Minutes were approved)
Hallam (PSE). - Madam President, on a point of order.
I just wish to draw the attention of this House to the agenda for this week, particular the agenda for Friday, when the only item on the agenda is the Hallam report...
Donnelly, Alan (PSE). - Madam President, on a point of order.
It concerns the Rules of this House.
