One of the important things which I would hope that the Commission will take away from our debate this evening is the way in which national administrations - I have talked about the British experience but, from comparing notes with other colleagues I understand it is just as bad in other countries - use Brussels and the European Commission as an excuse.
President - The Commissioner, who has been listening patiently, may now reply.
I would like to concentrate attention on paragraphs 10 and II of Mr Garosci's report. Paragraph 10 states that the distributive trades, small and mediumsized enterprises, suffer disproportionately from over-regulation as a result both of European Community directives and of national regulations.
I would like to expand a little bit on that point.
Papoutsis, Member of the Commission. - (EL) Mr President, I would like to thank you for showing special forbearance as regards time this evening and for allowing a substantial debate to be held with substantial contributions from all those who spoke.
