These hopes were once more destroyed by the inflexible attitude of Raouf Denktash.
It is quite unacceptable for Denktash to call for a cessation of the membership talks between the Union and Cyprus.
It is equaUy unacceptable for the Turkish Government and the illegal regime in the occupied part of Cyprus to threaten annexation by Turkey of the occupied part, if membership of the EU by Cyprus should take place.
B4-0790/97 by Mr Hatzidakis, on behalf of the Group of the European People's Party, on the political situation following the UN-sponsored talks on Cyprus in Troutbeck and Montreux;
