Monfils (ELDR). - (FR) Mr President, even if it is a compromise, this resolution on Cyprus is worthwhUe since on the one hand it condemns the blocking of negotiations, attributable to the Turkish Cypriots, and the new attempts at intimidation by Turkey, and, on the other hand, it reiterates Europe's desire to undertake from the start of 1998 negotiations on membership with the single recognized government that of the Republic of Cyprus.
